"""cycle60g - JANUARY, the Round 4 campaign
champion R423-PJW written as a live rule (app panel
format, following the other ports in this series).

NOT VALIDATED \u2014 campaign champion R423-PJW, live
port built and installed by user order 2026-11-13;
live replay verified EXACT (DISC 635 picks / 429
wins / +7,567.06; AUDIT 180 picks / 110 wins /
+1,003.20; combined DD 351.96 against the filed
frame record, pick-for-pick); blocker: the locked
screen FAILS \u2014 AUDIT win 61.11% < 70% (110 of
the 126 wins the screen needs at 180 picks,
distance 16), so the \u00a79 / EC22 battery never
ran and nothing about this design is validated.

PROVENANCE. Design R423-PJW, Round 4 campaign round
R4-023 (round4_campaign/r023_jan/: SLATE.md,
GRADING_R4_023.md, per_year_table.csv, research
module cycle_r423pjw.py, mask hash
aea5018713b16928). The design is the M5 validation
series' January champion M5R114A05 (grade98
eligibility + grade114 cell table + D1W rechoice +
agreement fill "second_mg") with three declared
changes, frozen in the rounds' SLATE.md files
before any AUDIT read: (1) the D1W step of the
single tier-1-intersection-certified cell (EURNZD,
13:00 UTC, SELL, tercile 2) is set to 2.0 in place
of 3.0, with eligibility and stability rebuilt
from the patched step map exactly as the champion
build rebuilds them; (2) the fill is the WDIV-NAME
form: both nominators' candidate lists are
re-sorted by (overlap, champion rank), the overlap
of the candidate cell's DISC-fitted losing-week
set (LOSE_WEEKS below) with the running book's
currently-losing ISO week numbers inside the era
segment; (3) the PROTECTION clause P: per era
segment and calendar year the fill tracks the
running (picks, wins) of committed picks; a year
is protected at a slot when it has >= 1 committed
pick and its running win rate is <= T_FRACTION
(51/83 = 61.45%, the champion's weakest
discovery-year win rate, DISC-fitted at R4-023
stage 1); at a protected slot where the WDIV-NAME
pick list differs from the champion-order
("hook-off") pick list computed from the same
pre-slot state, the re-deal is refused \u2014 the
hook-off list is committed instead \u2014 whenever
the WDIV list would leave the year's win rate
lower than the hook-off list would. Filed
protection log: 58 slots where the orderings
differed, 24 protected, 7 refusals.

THE RULE (as filed, constants embedded below).
Slots: January weekdays at UTC hours (11, 13, 17)
= 17:30 / 19:30 / 23:30 MMT. Entry = close of the
M15 bar ending at the slot; ATR14 (M15, pips);
TP = SL = step x ATR (RR 1:1), step in {2.0, 3.0};
SL-first in the same bar; 48h cap at the close of
the 192nd bar; cost 2.5 pips all-in. Volatility
tercile from H1 ATR14 against the embedded DISC
pair reference (ATRH_REF, unchanged from the
champion port). N1 eligibility: the row's
conditioned cell (symbol, hour, side, tercile,
step) clears rung s2 (cond exp >= 1.5, cond
n >= 30; uncond exp >= 1.0, uncond n >= 15) and
the D1W step test on the PATCHED map; N2 = N1
plus STAB1 split-half stability (both DISC halves
n >= 5, expectancy > 0). CELLS below holds, per
key, (N1, N2, cond_n, cond_exp, cond_win) of the
patched build (extract_pjw.py; the extraction's
frame control reproduces the filed book exactly).
Fill: see the FillState docstring.

BASIS / PORT NOTES. Candidate generation is
candle-native (inherited from the champion port
cycle60g, whose candle reproduction of the
filed universe was proven row-exact), with ONE
construction rule carried from the filed
universe builder (round86 gen_univ86): the
builder loaded each January in a [Dec 27, Feb 4)
window and created no row whose full 192-bar
path fell outside it, so the filed universe is
empty at the nine Jan-31 slots of 2019 / 2020 /
2025 whose paths cross the Feb-4 window end over
a weekend. This module applies the same rule in
_slot_rows: when the provided bar series covers
that Feb 4, a symbol contributes no rows at a
slot whose 192nd bar would start at or after
Feb 4 00:00 UTC. In live panels the series ends
at the current bar, the rule is inert, and the
module trades those slots \u2014 the same accepted
live form as the champion port. Rows are
generated only at steps {2.0, 3.0}: under the
patched step test no other step can be eligible,
so no pick can differ. The DISC second-pick gate
reads the candidate's realised net, computable
offline at the slot; in the app's live path live
slots are never in the DISC era (era is "disc"
only for slot years <= 2023, which occur only in
offline driving). A pick whose exit is not yet
resolvable blocks its symbol until
resolve_pending settles it (the live form of the
1-open-per-symbol law).
"""

